==============================================================================
SELF-CAUGHT BUG DISCLOSURE (this referee's own script, not the front's):
An earlier version of this script's arc-reconstruction walked FORWARD
via pi from each source s (s, pi(s), pi(pi(s)), ...) to build ARC(s).
This is backward: per ATTEMPT.md Section 1.2, position L_s (the LAST
position of ARC(s)) is the source itself, i.e. ARC(s) consists of s's
pi-PREDECESSORS, not successors. The forward-walk bug misattributed
points between arcs and produced spurious T != O+sum V_s 'failures'
at (n=4,K=2): 44/384 configs failing bookkeeping under the buggy
version, ALL 384 passing after the fix (walk pi^{-1} backward from s
instead). This was a bug in this adversarial script, not evidence
against the theorem -- caught and fixed before drawing any
conclusion, exactly the discipline the front itself models.
==============================================================================

